# REQUIRES: python-api
# What a start of an activation gives the entry (D[start-arguments], #326),
# Inputs/python_start_arguments.py, on the CPU: a sequence of starts against
# a simulation whose starts copy and convert every array anew, in double and
# mixed precision, with every conversion that is taken as kept made anew and
# compared and every buffer handed without a copy compared at the end of its
# activation (MDRT_CHECK_KEPT_TUPLES); and a byte of such a buffer written
# over, which that comparison finds.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: env MDRT_CHECK_KEPT_TUPLES=1 %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_start_arguments.py sequence %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU %t | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_start_arguments.py spoil %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPOIL
# CHECK: CPU Double: {{[0-9]+}} states, energies, and derivatives over {{[0-9]+}} calls that begin activations (steps, gradient() again, an evaluation, updates of each tunable, a commit of the charges and of the state, a second simulation of the program, a checkpoint with a run continued from it, and a frame evaluator) equal those of a simulation whose starts copy every array anew, to the bit; {{[0-9]+}} arrays handed without a copy at each start, {{[0-9]+}} conversions kept, each made anew and compared, and every buffer handed compared at the end of its activation
# CHECK: CPU Mixed: {{[0-9]+}} states
# CHECK: start arguments sequence CPU passed
# SPOIL: CPU: a byte of the masses that the entry took without a copy, written over, ends the process at the end of the activation under the variable, naming it, and is not looked for without it
# SPOIL: start arguments spoil CPU passed
